{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_1d_zero_grad_central",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady 1-D linear advection u_t = -c D(u,x) + c dGdx on the unit interval [0, 1] with no-flux walls, discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/central_D1_zero_grad_bc (2nd-order centered interior, 2nd-order one-sided zero-gradient faces). Manufactured STEADY solution u*(x) = cos(2 pi x) with the exactly matching steady forcing c dGdx, dGdx = g'(x) = -2 pi sin(2 pi x) (the analytic derivative of u*), so the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 and u(t) = u* for all t; the discrete field drifts only by the spatial truncation error of the operator, which is what the assertions and the convergence sweep measure (forced-steady MMS: observed L2/Linf order = operator order = 2). BC COMPATIBILITY (why cos(2 pi x)): u* is domain-periodic, so every ODD derivative vanishes at both walls (u*_x = -2 pi sin(2 pi x) and u*_xxx = (2 pi)^3 sin(2 pi x) are zero at x=0 and x=1); the rule's 2nd-order one-sided face has local truncation -(dx^2/3) u*_xxx(wall) + O(dx^3), so with u*_xxx(wall)=0 the faces are superconvergent and the global error is the clean interior O(dx^2). OBSERVATION WINDOW (why t=0.02, shorter than latlon's t=0.2): the both-ends one-sided closure of a CENTERED advection operator is only weakly stable — its semi-discrete spectrum carries a small O(dx)-scale positive real part (a mild boundary mode), unlike latlon's genuinely stable no-flux pole rows — so the truncation-driven drift is measured over a short window in which it stays dominated by the O(dx^2) spatial error rather than the slowly growing boundary transient (confirmed: L2/Linf observed order 2.0 across N=16..128 at t=0.02; the order degrades toward 1 only for observation windows several times longer). The measured order is a property of the semi-discrete operator and is independent of the temporal integrator tolerance. GRID CONTRACT WIRING (grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm) is fulfilled for [0, 1]: x0 = 0 (parameter) and dx = 1/N (an observed dividing by the metaparameter name N, substituted at load per esm-spec 9.7.6, so the convergence sweep's loader-API rebinding of N keeps dx consistent). The ic, the dGdx forcing, and the test references spell x_i = x0 + (i - 1/2) dx inline with load-foldable scalars (0 + (i - 1/2)(1/N)); the build-time 6.6.5/ic/observed cellwise evaluation is scope-free, so build-time coordinate expressions fold from literals and metaparameters alone (never the free-name x_coord template). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_zero_grad_central/golden/errors.json.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_1d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Fornberg, B. (1988). Generation of finite difference formulas on arbitrarily spaced grids. Mathematics of Computation 51(184), 699-706.",
        "doi": "10.1090/S0025-5718-1988-0935077-0"
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "Advection": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/rules/central_D1_zero_grad_bc.esm"
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the x index set."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed. Multiplies both the discretized derivative and the manufactured forcing, so the steady MMS balance holds for any value."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left domain edge a = 0 (unit interval): the grid's x0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_1d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Grid spacing (b - a)/N = 1/N: the grid's dx free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. N is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so loader-API rebinding for the convergence sweep keeps dx consistent."
        },
        "dGdx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^4",
          "shape": [
            "x"
          ],
          "description": "Analytic derivative of the manufactured solution: dGdx(x) = g'(x) = -2 pi sin(2 pi x). Constant in time; c dGdx is the manufactured forcing that holds u* = cos(2 pi x) steady. Cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N are spelled inline from literals and the metaparameter name N (build-time-foldable; never the free-name x_coord template)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "cos",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  6.283185307179586,
                  {
                    "op": "aggregate",
                    "output_idx": [
                      "i"
                    ],
                    "args": [],
                    "ranges": {
                      "i": {
                        "from": "x"
                      }
                    },
                    "expr": {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "i",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "N"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "c"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "x"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "c",
                  "dGdx"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "N"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dGdx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                -6.283185307179586,
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        6.283185307179586,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_zero_grad_central",
          "description": "Manufactured steady solution u*(x) = cos(2 pi x) with c = 1. Derivation: the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_x + c u*_x = 0 with u*_x = dGdx = -2 pi sin(2 pi x), so u(t) = u* exactly; the discrete drift is the pure spatial truncation of central_D1_zero_grad_bc. u* is domain-periodic, so its odd derivatives vanish at both no-flux walls and the 2nd-order one-sided faces are superconvergent (metadata.description), leaving the clean interior O(dx^2). References evaluate at cell centers x_i = 0 + (i - 1/2)/N, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.02 assertion bounds the truncation-driven drift against the SAME steady reference; the window is short because the centered both-ends one-sided operator is only weakly stable (metadata.description), so the drift stays O(dx^2)-dominated (well under the 0.01 bound at the default N=64, falling at order 2). Exact per-resolution errors are pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_1d_zero_grad_central/golden/errors.json.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.02
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.02,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.01
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "cos",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      6.283185307179586,
                      {
                        "op": "aggregate",
                        "output_idx": [
                          "i"
                        ],
                        "args": [],
                        "ranges": {
                          "i": {
                            "from": "x"
                          }
                        },
                        "expr": {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "i",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "N"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
